# Feature Documentation (`docs/`)

When creating or updating a payroll feature in routes, hooks, queries, api-services, or components, keep `docs/` in sync in the same change.

## What to document

- Purpose of the feature and when a user encounters it
- Routes (`src/routes/...`) and hooks (`use-<feature>`)
- HRIS endpoints (`api-services` method → Nest path)
- Auth/permission rules (who can call what; API is the security boundary)
- Env vars or setup steps if any

## Where to put it

- **Update an existing doc** when the topic already fits.
- **Add a new `docs/<feature-name>.md`** when there is no clear home — lowercase kebab-case.
- QA cases still go under `docs/qa/<feature>.test-cases.md`.

## How to write it

Keep docs actionable: what it does, real paths, real function names.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->

## Release payslip

- Route: `src/routes/dashboard/payslips/$id.tsx`
- Hook: `useReleasePayslip` (`src/hooks/use-payslips.ts`)
- Service: `payslipsService.release` → `POST /api/payslips/:id/release`
```

## Checklist

1. Did this change introduce or alter user-facing or API behavior?
2. Is there an existing `docs/*.md` to update, or do we need a new file?
3. Are routes, services, and auth called out with real paths/names?
4. Did you also update `docs/qa/<feature>.test-cases.md`?
